# DATASET: Sort-of-CLEVR  (the only dataset this script touches -- generated
# once, on demand, by the first run that needs it)
# 41 runs, ~32 GPU-h sequential on one GPU.
# WHY: THE decisive batch -- the identity/anchors claim is a rate claim: anchors_only to n~14, cells_only n~8, identity n~13, canonical n~28; the matched-encoder arm rides along (cheap, same dataset)
#     local  : bash bash_scripts/run_soc_1_assembly
#     on vast: python scripts/vast/vast_run.py auto bash_scripts/run_soc_1_assembly
# Runs of one cell share a cfg_hash in wandb -- group by it to pool draws
